# Runtime-suspend ONLY the Qualcomm DWC3 glue (the USB controller's platform
# device), never the USB devices below it.
#
# Why: an active DWC3 holds a 1 GB/s USB-to-DDR interconnect vote in every RPMh
# bucket, including the sleep set, which blocks the DDR low-power tiers while
# the port is idle (awake drain). System suspend already drops that vote via
# dwc3_qcom_pm_suspend regardless of this rule, so s2idle is unaffected.
#
# Why NOT a blanket "every USB device -> auto": ArmadaOS tried that (0656c6f)
# and hubs autosuspended too, powering off their downstream ports, so input
# devices behind a hub/dock re-enumerated on resume and froze for ~1 s
# (armada issue #302). Leaf USB devices stay at the kernel default
# power/control=on, so a hub/dock keeps its ports powered.
#
# Ported verbatim from ArmadaOS system_files/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/
# 60-armada-usb-autosuspend.rules as of armada 98d8f53 (2026-09-15,
# "fix(udev): only autosuspend the DWC3 controller, not whole USB tree").
# Holodor 2026-09-20 (upstream sweep item U1). We had no USB power/control
# rule before this; nothing is replaced.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", KERNEL=="*.usb", DRIVERS=="dwc3-qcom", ATTR{power/control}="auto"
